    "v7_rules": "Sections ordered by CHAIN ascending (byte order). Within a section the (PUBKEY,SIG) pairs are ordered by PUBKEY ascending. The bundle SNAPSHOT_BLOCK is the MAX of the sections SECTION_SNAPSHOT_BLOCK. Each section omits NETWORK; the indexer rebuilds every section canonical (XCHECKPOINT|CHAIN|NETWORK|...) with the header NETWORK. The fixture below deliberately lists sections and one signature list OUT of order so both producer and parser tests prove they apply the ordering rules rather than echo fixture order. Retired versions 0/3/4/5 (one anchor per chain) were removed from this file on 2026-08-28 by operator ruling (pre-launch, superseded wires deleted)."
